{"id": "10th-u6-q141", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "single_choice", "level": "standard", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "10", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "unit_6", "lesson_id": "karupporul_uripporul", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "karupporul_definition", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "அகப்பொருள் இலக்கணத்தில் ஒரு நிலத்திற்குரிய தெய்வம், மக்கள், உணவு, விலங்கு, பூ, மரம், தொழில் முதலான இயற்கைக் கூறுகள் எவ்வாறு அழைக்கப்படுகின்றன?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கருப்பொருள்", "B": "முதற்பொருள்", "C": "உரிப்பொருள்", "D": "பொருள்கோள்"}, "explanation": "ஒரு நிலத்தின் வாழ்வியல் பண்பாட்டையும் இயற்கை சூழலையும் வெளிப்படுத்தும் தெய்வம், மக்கள், உணவு, தொழில் முதலானவை \"கருப்பொருள்\" எனப்படுகின்றன."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In Agapporul, what collective category encompasses regional deities, inhabitants, fauna, flora, food, and crafts of a landscape?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Karupporul (Regional environment and cultural fixtures)", "B": "Mudharporul", "C": "Uripporul", "D": "Porulkol"}, "explanation": "Karupporul signifies the native matrix of deities, fauna, flora, food, and occupations."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "10", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 142